	(text_box "Hall Sensor Inputs\n\nAssume VH required by motor hall sensors is 5V, but expose pad to switch to 3V3, if desired (XOR)\n\nUM2896 5.4: Use CH1-3 of TIM3 (PB4, PB5, PB0) for HA, HB, HC (built-in XOR)\n\nOptional MOTOR_TEMP pin if chosen motor provides winding temps (Note: This is different from the one in Control sheet)\n\nDC12_IN6 on PC0 used for MOTOR_TEMP based on availability\n\nNotes: \n- Only open-drain sensors are supported so added pull-up resistors and diodes to clamp voltage at 3V3 to protect MCU\n- Active 5V push-pull hall sensors are NOT supported, as the pins couldn't be mapped such that they are 5V-tolerant"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 132.08 86.36 0)
		(size 35.56 58.4199)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "058252ef-e6db-4954-9c3b-e1283fca4622")
	)
	(text_box "Serial (JST-PH)\n\n- Uses USART1_TX (PA9) & USART1_RX (PA10), which are 5V-tolerant\n- For sk8's Flipsky VX1's receiver module (JST-PH)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 213.36 86.4126 0)
		(size 22.86 25.3474)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "308dfcba-932b-499f-b5bf-98aa49e75756")
	)
	(text_box "Voltage Monitor\n\nMost power-related signals exposed through test points near pins"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 213.36 147.32 0)
		(size 22.86 30.48)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "66f0c9e3-cd91-4c8d-adc2-87ad6d812bd6")
	)
	(text_box "Programming (STDC14)\n\nExpects STLINK-V3, so exposes pins through STDC14 connector\n\nUses MCU's internal VDD to determine if it's on "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 220.98 17.78 0)
		(size 15.24 30.5285)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "671752fe-1c24-4858-aa49-3ccf7df1dc38")
	)
	(text_box "2.54 Comm (2.54mm Pitch Header)\n\nSerial and ADC exposed twice (once with their own JST connectors, and another while combined with regular male pins)\n\nFor debugging"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 213.36 114.3 0)
		(size 23.114 30.48)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "6841050d-9026-4a68-97e2-30ab89861a9d")
	)
	(text_box "Phase Outputs\n\nSimilar idea to Battery Input, but for final prototype, 16 AWG wire will use bullet connectors"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 35.56 0)
		(size 60.96 12.7)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "945f6eda-bc12-4081-8fe6-fe20c007c0d0")
	)
	(text_box "I2C (Optional)\n\nUses I2C1_SDA (PB9), I2C1_SCL (PA15)\n\nMay expect a display? Just exposing it to future-proof"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 142.24 147.32 0)
		(size 25.4 30.48)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "aa919859-994f-4f30-bc1b-c28e2908e2ff")
	)
	(text_box "Throttle (JST-XH)\n\n- Uses ADC2 or ADC12_IN7 (PC1)\n- For bike's thumb throttle (wire cut off & stripped)\n- Expects 5V ADC for full range\n- Can also use an external pot"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 218.44 50.8 0)
		(size 17.78 33.0199)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ab53f14c-20c4-4a71-b0b6-072eec2a4dff")
	)
	(text_box "Battery Input\n\nUse a footprint with a pad AND large plated holes\n\nFor intial testing, will solder a screw terminal block\n\nFor final prototype, will solder 16 AWG wire (for PowerPole)\n\nE: new addition, using 10 AWG wire with studs and the LCA10-10-L CONN TERM RECT TONG 10 AWG #10 connection"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 104.14 50.8 0)
		(size 63.5 33.02)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c233b16a-6aa2-4b57-a6fd-6e5b34b59832")
	)
	(text_box "SPI (Optional)\n\nUses SPI1 (PA4-7), which are NOT 5V-tolerant\n\nOnly supports 3.3V TTL\n\nMay expect a rotary encoder (alternative to hall sensor)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 55.88 147.3599 0)
		(size 35.56 30.4401)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type none)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c3d6a2be-f335-4451-a94f-7d53e5fe76b9")
	)
	(text_box "Power Switch\n\nClose the slide switch to drive EN_UVLO high on LM74502\n\nR_limit=10k (0805) both protects against shorts and is part of divider circuit (see PWR net in Power sheet)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 17.78 0)
		(size 60.96 17.7799)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
